WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
This is Beverly Hills, and here come the Beverly Hillbillies.

00:07.000 --> 00:34.000
And here come the Beverly Hillbillies.

00:34.000 --> 00:44.000
Well, come on, let's find that house we bought.

00:44.000 --> 00:47.000
House they bought?

00:47.000 --> 00:49.000
In Beverly Hills?

00:49.000 --> 00:52.000
Whoa, wait a minute, hold it!

00:52.000 --> 00:57.000
How could a bunch of hillbillies possibly buy a mansion like this?

00:57.000 --> 01:22.000
Let's take them back to their home and see how this whole thing started.

01:22.000 --> 01:27.000
Hey, kid, you gotta do something about that young'un of yours.

01:27.000 --> 01:28.000
How'd that happen?

01:28.000 --> 01:30.000
Fighting with a bobcat.

01:30.000 --> 01:31.000
Get hurt?

01:31.000 --> 01:32.000
I reckon so.

01:32.000 --> 01:36.000
It went limping off on three legs.

01:36.000 --> 01:40.000
I swear, I don't know what I'm gonna do about that girl.

01:40.000 --> 01:43.000
Well, the first thing to do is to get her into a dress.

01:43.000 --> 01:46.000
She's getting too big to be wearing man's duds.

01:46.000 --> 01:50.000
Looky here, she's done popped the buttons off of her shirt again.

01:50.000 --> 01:55.000
Well, honey, make yourself proud with the shoulders thrown back.

01:55.000 --> 02:00.000
It ain't her shoulders that's popping these buttons.

02:00.000 --> 02:03.000
Fully grown up, rounded out, female won't.

02:03.000 --> 02:05.000
Time she start acting like one.

02:05.000 --> 02:10.000
Well, one day some boy will come along and start courting her.

02:10.000 --> 02:12.000
They came courting when she was 12.

02:12.000 --> 02:14.000
What did she do?

02:14.000 --> 02:18.000
She whopped the tar out of them.

02:18.000 --> 02:19.000
Well, it ain't fitting.

02:19.000 --> 02:24.000
A girl running around as wild as a cougar, wrestling, fighting and hunting.

02:24.000 --> 02:26.000
She ought to be doing woman's work.

02:26.000 --> 02:30.000
Happen me with the steel.

02:30.000 --> 02:33.000
Yeah, well, I'll speak to her.

02:33.000 --> 02:38.000
Oh, that reminds me.

02:38.000 --> 02:43.000
Better go down and stomp out the fire under that mass.

02:43.000 --> 02:45.000
Hold on now, Granny.

02:45.000 --> 02:49.000
You ain't going to stomp out no fire like that, are you?

02:49.000 --> 02:51.000
Oh, of course not.

02:51.000 --> 02:56.000
Don't want to burn the shoes.

02:56.000 --> 02:58.000
Pa?

02:58.000 --> 02:59.000
Granny?

02:59.000 --> 03:02.000
Somebody open the door.

03:02.000 --> 03:05.000
Howdy, Pa.

03:05.000 --> 03:08.000
What you got there?

03:08.000 --> 03:10.000
Stranger.

03:10.000 --> 03:11.000
Where'd you get him?

03:11.000 --> 03:14.000
I binged him with a rock.

03:14.000 --> 03:16.000
He was skulking around down by the slough.

03:16.000 --> 03:18.000
Figured he might be a revenue.

03:18.000 --> 03:20.000
He ain't no revenue bird.

03:20.000 --> 03:22.000
Then can I keep him?

03:22.000 --> 03:24.000
Of course not.

03:24.000 --> 03:25.000
Well, I caught him.

03:25.000 --> 03:26.000
Doesn't matter.

03:26.000 --> 03:28.000
Well, he won't be no trouble.

03:28.000 --> 03:29.000
I could keep him out in the smokehouse.

03:29.000 --> 03:34.000
Ellie Mae, you can't keep people like they were dogs and cats.

03:34.000 --> 03:48.000
Oh, oh, oh, oh, that's fart.

03:48.000 --> 03:49.000
Who's that?

03:49.000 --> 03:52.000
Some fella Ellie found nosing around.

03:52.000 --> 03:55.000
Binging with the rock so it'd be easier to tilt.

03:55.000 --> 03:58.000
They're fellas from the petroleum company.

03:58.000 --> 03:59.000
What's a petroleum?

03:59.000 --> 04:00.000
I don't know.

04:00.000 --> 04:04.000
He asked me if he could do some wildcatting down by the slough.

04:04.000 --> 04:05.000
I said, help yourself.

04:05.000 --> 04:07.000
We're glad to get rid of the critters.

04:07.000 --> 04:08.000
What'd he say?

04:08.000 --> 04:09.000
He kind of laughed.

04:09.000 --> 04:14.000
The last I saw him, there ain't no wildcats down there at that slough.

04:14.000 --> 04:16.000
It's too full of oil.

04:16.000 --> 04:22.000
Oh, oh, what happened?

04:22.000 --> 04:23.000
Where am I?

04:23.000 --> 04:25.000
This here is the Clampett place.

04:25.000 --> 04:28.000
I'm Jed Clampett, my youngin' Ellie Mae and Granny.

04:28.000 --> 04:31.000
Granny says you've been doing some wildcatting.

04:31.000 --> 04:32.000
There's no need to.

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
Mr. Clampett, that swamp of yours is full of oil.

04:35.000 --> 04:37.000
I could have told you that.

04:37.000 --> 04:39.000
Well, my company would like to pump it out.

04:39.000 --> 04:43.000
Yeah, I'd like that too, but I just can't afford to have a ton.

04:43.000 --> 04:45.000
Oh, no, no, you don't understand.

04:45.000 --> 04:48.000
You see, you wouldn't have to pay for it.

04:48.000 --> 04:51.000
Oh, I don't take favors from strangers.

04:51.000 --> 04:57.000
No, no, no, Mr. Clampett, you see, you're a very rich man.

04:57.000 --> 05:00.000
How big a rock did you bean him with?

05:00.000 --> 05:03.000
No bigger than a hedge apple.

05:03.000 --> 05:05.000
Listen, I've got to call my office in Tulsa.

05:05.000 --> 05:07.000
Have you got a telephone?

05:07.000 --> 05:08.000
A what?

05:08.000 --> 05:10.000
A telephone.

05:10.000 --> 05:12.000
Oh, maybe one of your neighbors has one.

05:12.000 --> 05:17.000
It's a, uh, well, down in this country, it's probably a box attached to the wall.

05:17.000 --> 05:23.000
And, uh, you talk into it, and they can hear you in Tulsa.

05:23.000 --> 05:27.000
Maybe you'd better sit down for a spell.

05:27.000 --> 05:29.000
Oh, I haven't time.

05:29.000 --> 05:31.000
Listen, where's the nearest airfield?

05:31.000 --> 05:33.000
Airfield?

05:33.000 --> 05:40.000
You know, Granny, that's, uh, when them airfields sets up in the air.

05:40.000 --> 05:42.000
Oh, never mind, I'll find it myself.

05:42.000 --> 05:45.000
Listen, now don't you sell that swamp till you hear from me.

05:45.000 --> 05:49.000
I'm flying to Tulsa.

05:49.000 --> 06:03.000
Now he thinks he's got wings.

06:03.000 --> 06:06.000
Morning, Granny.

06:06.000 --> 06:10.000
Wash them buttons, child.

06:10.000 --> 06:14.000
Granny!

06:14.000 --> 06:18.000
Them fake dealers got into the car.

06:18.000 --> 06:22.000
Did they drink much?

06:22.000 --> 06:23.000
I reckon they did.

06:23.000 --> 06:27.000
This here little fellow was kicking blue blazers out of the mule.

06:27.000 --> 06:29.000
That's the trouble with Razorbacks.

06:29.000 --> 06:35.000
They's such a mean drunk.

06:35.000 --> 06:49.000
This wouldn't happen if you'd stay in the house where you belong.

06:49.000 --> 06:51.000
There it is, Mr. Brewster.

06:51.000 --> 06:56.000
From the testing surveys, I'd say that's gonna be one of the richest pools since East Texas.

06:56.000 --> 06:58.000
News like this is bound to get out.

06:58.000 --> 07:04.000
Let's go down and get Pappen's name on a deal.

07:04.000 --> 07:06.000
Where's the gun? Where's the gun?

07:06.000 --> 07:07.000
Oh, there, there, there.

07:07.000 --> 07:08.000
What's the matter?

07:08.000 --> 07:10.000
You want to see what just flew over Blueberry Ridge?

07:10.000 --> 07:11.000
What?

07:11.000 --> 07:14.000
That dad blamed this biggest bird you ever laid eyes on.

07:14.000 --> 07:16.000
Probably just an overgrown chicken hawk.

07:16.000 --> 07:17.000
Chicken hawk nothing.

07:17.000 --> 07:18.000
That thing could make off with a hog.

07:18.000 --> 07:24.000
Hurry up, put that gun together.

07:24.000 --> 07:26.000
No room to land near the cabin, Mr. Brewster.

07:26.000 --> 07:28.000
It's too rocky and hilly.

07:28.000 --> 07:30.000
Then let's get the sling ready to be lowered.

07:30.000 --> 07:32.000
Well, Mr. Brewster, that might be dangerous.

07:32.000 --> 07:37.000
Hang the danger. We're going to be the first oil company down there if it kills you.

07:37.000 --> 07:38.000
Me?

07:38.000 --> 07:43.000
Don't worry. If it's safe, I'll follow you.

07:43.000 --> 07:45.000
Granny, I see it. There it is.

07:45.000 --> 07:49.000
Land of mercy. Look at that.

07:49.000 --> 07:50.000
What you doing, Granny?

07:50.000 --> 07:58.000
That thing's only got one claw, but dang if it ain't grabbed up a man.

07:58.000 --> 08:01.000
Hurry, Pa. It's my stranger.

08:01.000 --> 08:02.000
Where is it?

08:02.000 --> 08:14.000
Just below the house. I'll give it on to the side.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.000
You feel it, Granny?

08:16.000 --> 08:33.000
No, but I may have dropped that stranger.

08:33.000 --> 08:36.000
Jeff, stop this thing. Stop it.

08:36.000 --> 08:38.000
Oh, God, help me.

08:38.000 --> 08:40.000
Granny. Granny.

08:40.000 --> 08:42.000
Yes, Jeff.

08:42.000 --> 08:49.000
Granny, grab a hold of something and hang on. Cousin Pearl and an overgrown son of hers is headed right for the cabin in that old truck.

08:49.000 --> 08:53.000
Heaven protect us.

08:53.000 --> 09:00.000
Oh, Jeff, no.

09:00.000 --> 09:02.000
Did they hit us, kid?

09:02.000 --> 09:07.000
No, but I think they sure warmed the chicken house.

09:07.000 --> 09:15.000
Oh, Jeff, I'm sure sorry about the chicken house, but nobody got hurt.

09:15.000 --> 09:19.000
Jeff, I told you to get rid of them worn-out brakes.

09:19.000 --> 09:24.000
I did, Ma. It's how come we ain't got none.

09:24.000 --> 09:28.000
Get on out and let the chicken house back on its foundation.

09:28.000 --> 09:29.000
Jeff?

09:29.000 --> 09:30.000
Yeah?

09:30.000 --> 09:36.000
Jeff, Ellie Mae came running over to my place and she said you sold the swamp to some once company.

09:36.000 --> 09:41.000
Well, yeah, I guess I did.

09:41.000 --> 09:44.000
What did they pay you for it?

09:44.000 --> 09:46.000
Oh, they ain't paid me nothing yet.

09:46.000 --> 09:48.000
That rooster fella said he'd bring the money later.

09:48.000 --> 09:51.000
How much they gonna pay you?

09:51.000 --> 09:55.000
Well, he said that depends some on how much oil they could pump up.

09:55.000 --> 09:58.000
Well, he must have mentioned something. What was it?

09:58.000 --> 10:02.000
Now, Pearl, you know that old swamp was worth shots.

10:02.000 --> 10:07.000
You clamp it, you got slick it, and you're ashamed to admit it. That's just what I told him.

10:07.000 --> 10:09.000
Granny, how much they gonna pay him?

10:09.000 --> 10:12.000
All right, I'll tell you. He said it runs somewhere between 25 and 100.

10:12.000 --> 10:14.000
25 and 100?

10:14.000 --> 10:21.000
I know it don't sound like much, but Mr. Brewster seemed to set great store by the fact he's gonna pay me in some new kind of dollar.

10:21.000 --> 10:24.000
There ain't no new kind of dollar.

10:24.000 --> 10:31.000
Well, it's new to me. I've heard of gold dollars, silver dollars, paper dollars, but he says he's gonna pay me in, uh, what do you call them, Granny?

10:31.000 --> 10:35.000
Million dollars.

10:35.000 --> 10:37.000
Yeah, that's it.

10:37.000 --> 10:40.000
Million dollars?

10:40.000 --> 10:46.000
Yeah, I mean, he wrote the whole thing out on this piece of paper here. You can see for yourself. I don't know nothing about that.

10:46.000 --> 10:48.000
Let's see here.

10:48.000 --> 10:52.000
Thanks in heaven.

10:52.000 --> 10:54.000
Granny, give me the jug.

10:54.000 --> 10:56.000
It's empty, but I'll fetch some.

10:56.000 --> 11:00.000
I'll go, Granny.

11:00.000 --> 11:04.000
Jed, Jed!

11:04.000 --> 11:06.000
You're a millionaire.

11:06.000 --> 11:08.000
A millionaire?

11:08.000 --> 11:13.000
Yeah, that's what that Brewster fella kept calling me. I didn't know just how to take it.

11:13.000 --> 11:15.000
You mean you're rich.

11:15.000 --> 11:16.000
Me?

11:16.000 --> 11:20.000
The richest man in these hills. Maybe in the whole state.

11:20.000 --> 11:28.000
Oh, Jed, you can have anything you want, do anything you want, go any place you want.

11:28.000 --> 11:33.000
Yeah, that's another thing he kept saying. He said he reckoned I'd be moving away from here soon.

11:33.000 --> 11:36.000
What do you think, Pearl? Do you think I ought to move?

11:36.000 --> 11:44.000
Jed, how can you even ask? Look around you. You're eight miles from your nearest neighbor.

11:44.000 --> 11:49.000
You overrun with skunks, possums, coyotes, bobcats.

11:49.000 --> 11:53.000
You use kerosene lamps for light. You cook on a wood stove summer and winter.

11:53.000 --> 11:58.000
You're drinking homemade moonshine, washing with homemade lye soap.

11:58.000 --> 12:06.000
And your bathroom is 50 feet from the house and you ask, should you move?

12:06.000 --> 12:09.000
Yeah, I reckon you're right.

12:09.000 --> 12:19.000
Man be a dang fool, he always.

12:19.000 --> 12:26.000
There you are, Jed. You misunderstood me. I meant you should move away.

12:26.000 --> 12:28.000
And you know where I'd go if I was you?

12:28.000 --> 12:29.000
Where?

12:29.000 --> 12:31.000
California.

12:31.000 --> 12:33.000
California?

12:33.000 --> 12:38.000
Yes, the Beverly Hills, California.

12:38.000 --> 12:44.000
Jed, remember the time that your pa took us to Eureka Springs to see the movie picture?

12:44.000 --> 12:46.000
Yeah.

12:46.000 --> 12:52.000
Well, the actors that make them movie pictures live in Beverly Hills.

12:52.000 --> 12:53.000
Go on.

12:53.000 --> 12:55.000
Yes.

12:55.000 --> 12:57.000
Way doggie.

12:57.000 --> 12:59.000
Ain't that something?

12:59.000 --> 13:03.000
Living in the same neck of the woods as old town men.

13:03.000 --> 13:10.000
That's how I love it. And we could come visit you.

13:10.000 --> 13:13.000
You know what else they say about California?

13:13.000 --> 13:14.000
What?

13:14.000 --> 13:16.000
It don't get cold out there.

13:16.000 --> 13:18.000
What don't get cold out there?

13:18.000 --> 13:23.000
Nothing don't get cold out there. They don't have no snow or no ice.

13:23.000 --> 13:25.000
Can't they bring some in?

13:25.000 --> 13:29.000
They don't want it. That's why it be so good for Granny.

13:29.000 --> 13:34.000
Remember last winter when she slipped on the ice and broke her hip?

13:34.000 --> 13:40.000
Yeah, poor old woman. She was limping for two days.

13:40.000 --> 13:45.000
Well, that couldn't happen in California because they don't have no ice.

13:45.000 --> 13:47.000
How come?

13:47.000 --> 13:57.000
I don't know how come. But Granny sure like it. And we could visit you.

13:57.000 --> 14:00.000
You know what else they say about California?

14:00.000 --> 14:04.000
Maybe Jethro know how come there's no ice. He's going to school.

14:04.000 --> 14:06.000
We could ask him.

14:06.000 --> 14:08.000
Jethro?

14:08.000 --> 14:09.000
Yeah, Ma?

14:09.000 --> 14:10.000
Come over here.

14:10.000 --> 14:16.000
Speaking of school, Ellie May could get herself a fine education out there in Beverly Hills.

14:16.000 --> 14:18.000
Yeah, Ma?

14:18.000 --> 14:22.000
Your rich uncle's got a question he'd like to ask you.

14:22.000 --> 14:25.000
What rich uncle, Ma?

14:25.000 --> 14:27.000
Your rich uncle, Jade.

14:27.000 --> 14:33.000
Jethro, how come there's no ice in California?

14:33.000 --> 14:37.000
Don't look at me. I didn't take it.

14:37.000 --> 14:39.000
You didn't tell me there was no ice in it, Ma.

14:39.000 --> 14:40.000
Oh, get out of here.

14:40.000 --> 14:43.000
Well, you always... I don't know.

14:43.000 --> 14:49.000
You understand, Jade. Folks claim California's got it all beat.

14:49.000 --> 14:52.000
Why, things grow twice as big out there.

14:52.000 --> 14:57.000
Jethro would be a whopper, wouldn't he?

14:57.000 --> 15:02.000
He could help you move. He's awful handy at lifting and toting.

15:02.000 --> 15:05.000
And he could drive you out in my truck.

15:05.000 --> 15:08.000
I'll tell you what, Pearl. I'm going to have to study on this.

15:08.000 --> 15:13.000
When that Brewster fella comes back, I'll ask him what he thinks.

15:13.000 --> 15:16.000
Well, your cousin is right about that, Mr. Clampett.

15:16.000 --> 15:21.000
Beverly Hills is a choice residential area, and lots of millionaires do settle there.

15:21.000 --> 15:23.000
Folks like me, huh?

15:23.000 --> 15:26.000
Well, uh, millionaires.

15:26.000 --> 15:29.000
And movie stars, too.

15:29.000 --> 15:31.000
Is Tom Mix there?

15:31.000 --> 15:34.000
No. I'm afraid Mr. Mix is dead.

15:34.000 --> 15:36.000
Oh?

15:36.000 --> 15:39.000
Oh, yeah. What's the matter with me?

15:39.000 --> 15:45.000
Remember Pearl? He got shot at the end of that picture.

15:45.000 --> 15:53.000
Well, there are plenty of other movie stars, and that's where Jed wants to live. Ain't it, Jed?

15:53.000 --> 15:56.000
I do like the notion of living in the hills.

15:56.000 --> 15:58.000
Never could stay in flat country.

15:58.000 --> 16:01.000
Mr. Clampett, I think it only fair...

16:01.000 --> 16:06.000
That is? Well, I think you may have a wrong idea about Beverly Hills.

16:06.000 --> 16:07.000
Is that where you live?

16:07.000 --> 16:09.000
No. My home is in Tulsa.

16:09.000 --> 16:15.000
Well, see. Maybe you could get us a place there in your neighborhood.

16:15.000 --> 16:20.000
Mr. Clampett, let's not beat around the bush. You will love Beverly Hills.

16:20.000 --> 16:24.000
Then that's it. Can you steer Jed on to a good place?

16:24.000 --> 16:27.000
No. I can get the bank out there to handle it for him.

16:27.000 --> 16:37.000
I would like a nice big place with plenty of room for his kinfolk to visit him.

16:37.000 --> 16:42.000
I would like a nice roomy place if I could afford it.

16:42.000 --> 16:45.000
Oh, Mr. Clampett, with your money you can afford the Taj Mahal.

16:45.000 --> 16:48.000
Okay, I'll take it.

16:48.000 --> 16:51.000
Well, no. You see, I was just making a little joke.

16:51.000 --> 16:55.000
Oh. Well, go right ahead.

16:55.000 --> 17:05.000
Well, you see, the Taj Mahal is in India.

17:05.000 --> 17:13.000
Mr. Brewster, you're a nice fellow, but I've heard better jokes.

17:13.000 --> 17:15.000
Is the foreigner staying to supper?

17:15.000 --> 17:18.000
I'm ashamed to say I ain't asked him. How about it?

17:18.000 --> 17:20.000
Oh, I don't think so.

17:20.000 --> 17:22.000
Oh, no trouble. What are you cooking tonight, Granny?

17:22.000 --> 17:25.000
Mustard greens and possum innards.

17:25.000 --> 17:29.000
Mmm. Did you hear that, Mr. Brewster?

17:29.000 --> 17:31.000
Very clearly.

17:31.000 --> 17:33.000
Want to change your mind?

17:33.000 --> 17:35.000
Uh, not this time.

17:35.000 --> 17:39.000
Well, if you can happen to come back tomorrow, we'll be having leftovers.

17:39.000 --> 17:49.000
That's the thing about possum innards. It's just as good as second day.

17:49.000 --> 17:54.000
Ellie, if old Duke sits there with you, there ain't gonna be room for Granny.

17:54.000 --> 17:58.000
Oh, that's all right, Pa. Granny ain't gone.

17:58.000 --> 18:00.000
Who says she ain't?

18:00.000 --> 18:01.000
She says she ain't.

18:01.000 --> 18:03.000
That's right, Uncle Jed.

18:03.000 --> 18:10.000
She's just sitting on the back porch in her rocker, and she says that's as close to California as you're gonna get her.

18:10.000 --> 18:13.000
We'll see about that.

18:13.000 --> 18:17.000
Thank the boy he ain't got me the mule he's swimming for.

18:17.000 --> 18:24.000
He ain't never gonna get there.

18:24.000 --> 18:28.000
Now, what's all this nonsense about you ain't going to California?

18:28.000 --> 18:31.000
Ain't no license to it.

18:31.000 --> 18:36.000
If the good Lord had a wanted me in California, he'd a put me in California.

18:36.000 --> 18:38.000
Maybe he's just kidding around to it.

18:38.000 --> 18:42.000
The book says he moves in mysterious ways.

18:42.000 --> 18:49.000
Well, if he moves me, I'll go. But you and Big Jethro ain't a-budging me.

18:49.000 --> 18:53.000
Granny, this here Beverly Hills sounds like the kind of place you'd like.

18:53.000 --> 18:57.000
That Berichia fella says they got smogs out there.

18:57.000 --> 18:58.000
What's a smog?

18:58.000 --> 19:03.000
Well, me and Jethro figured out that's a small hog.

19:03.000 --> 19:05.000
And you heard what Pearl said.

19:05.000 --> 19:09.000
Ain't got no snow on fella, he's bought us a house in them Beverly Hills.

19:09.000 --> 19:11.000
He's in there 25 million to the gut there.

19:11.000 --> 19:13.000
Well, you just chase on out after it.

19:13.000 --> 19:15.000
I'm staying right here.

19:15.000 --> 19:19.000
And I ain't a-feared neither.

19:19.000 --> 19:22.000
Granny, I ain't a-leaving you here alone.

19:22.000 --> 19:35.000
And I ain't a-budging out of this rocker.

19:35.000 --> 19:38.000
Jethro, what does that sign say?

19:38.000 --> 19:41.000
It says Beverly Hills.

19:41.000 --> 19:44.000
You scared that, Granny? We're buyers.

19:44.000 --> 19:46.000
They call them hills?

19:46.000 --> 19:50.000
Why, we got moles that can push up higher ridges than that.

19:50.000 --> 19:52.000
Well, these ways ain't hills.

19:52.000 --> 20:04.000
We'll be among our kind of folks.

20:04.000 --> 20:11.000
This deposit of 25 million dollars to the account of J.D. Clampett.

20:11.000 --> 20:12.000
J.D.?

20:12.000 --> 20:15.000
As in Rockefeller.

20:15.000 --> 20:19.000
Elevates us to third position in capital assets.

20:19.000 --> 20:22.000
And assures our bank of...

20:22.000 --> 20:23.000
Come in.

20:23.000 --> 20:25.000
I'm sorry to interrupt, Mr. Drysdale.

20:25.000 --> 20:27.000
All right, Taylor.

20:27.000 --> 20:30.000
Well, are we all set to give the Clampetts a red carpet reception?

20:30.000 --> 20:33.000
Well, I'm afraid Mrs. Drysdale still isn't too happy, sir.

20:33.000 --> 20:35.000
Yes, I know.

20:35.000 --> 20:39.000
Oh, my wife is very upset that I got the estate next to ours for the Clampetts.

20:39.000 --> 20:41.000
Says I don't even know what kind of people they are.

20:41.000 --> 20:45.000
Do you?

20:45.000 --> 20:48.000
I know to the dollar what kind of people they are.

20:48.000 --> 20:50.000
They're my kind of people.

20:50.000 --> 20:53.000
Loaded.

20:53.000 --> 20:54.000
Taylor?

20:54.000 --> 20:56.000
Have the gardeners got the grounds in order?

20:56.000 --> 20:57.000
Yes, sir.

20:57.000 --> 20:59.000
But I'm afraid that's another thing your wife is upset about.

20:59.000 --> 21:00.000
Oh?

21:00.000 --> 21:03.000
Your gardeners have been working on their lawn all week.

21:03.000 --> 21:05.000
They've mowed it, trimmed it, fed it, clipped it.

21:05.000 --> 21:08.000
I don't care if they lather it and shave it.

21:08.000 --> 21:10.000
This is the most beautiful mansion in Beverly Hills.

21:10.000 --> 21:13.000
I want every square inch of ground within those walls and apple pie...

21:13.000 --> 21:17.000
Yes?

21:17.000 --> 21:19.000
Oh, hello, Margaret.

21:19.000 --> 21:22.000
No, dear, I'm very...

21:22.000 --> 21:24.000
What?

21:24.000 --> 21:27.000
Oh, good heavens, did you call the police?

21:27.000 --> 21:28.000
I'll be right there.

21:28.000 --> 21:29.000
What happened?

21:29.000 --> 21:32.000
The Clampett estate is being invaded by a band of outlaws.

21:32.000 --> 21:33.000
Invaded?

21:33.000 --> 21:42.000
Yes, they're holding the gardeners at gunpoint.

21:42.000 --> 21:45.000
Sure is lucky we come along when we did.

21:45.000 --> 21:46.000
That's the truth.

21:46.000 --> 21:48.000
The way they were slipping through that gate,

21:48.000 --> 21:54.000
another five minutes and that whole darn prison would have been empty.

21:54.000 --> 21:55.000
Getro?

21:55.000 --> 21:58.000
You sure that's a prison?

21:58.000 --> 22:03.000
Yeah, Uncle Jed, I seen pictures.

22:03.000 --> 22:07.000
Only thing is, how come there ain't no guards on them walls?

22:07.000 --> 22:10.000
Probably done them in with them knives and things.

22:10.000 --> 22:13.000
These killers, if I ever did see any,

22:13.000 --> 22:18.000
fine neighborhood we's moving into.

22:18.000 --> 22:19.000
You hear that?

22:19.000 --> 22:24.000
I'll dig in there as bobcats if they see us.

22:24.000 --> 22:25.000
Hey, I'm sorry.

22:25.000 --> 22:27.000
Somebody's called the law.

22:27.000 --> 22:33.000
I reckon he's going to be mighty grateful for what we done.

22:33.000 --> 22:39.000
Folks out here has got a strange way of showing they's grateful.

22:39.000 --> 22:41.000
You've locked up one of the richest men in the country.

22:41.000 --> 22:43.000
Mr. Clampett, I don't know how to apologize.

22:43.000 --> 22:46.000
I'm deeply humiliated.

22:46.000 --> 22:49.000
What have you cutthroat scum of J.D. Clampett?

22:49.000 --> 22:55.000
I'm Jed Clampett and I'd appreciate it if you'd let go of my Sunday shirt.

22:55.000 --> 22:57.000
You're J.D. Clampett, the oil millionaire?

22:57.000 --> 22:59.000
Yep, this here's my nephew Jethro.

22:59.000 --> 23:00.000
Howdy.

23:00.000 --> 23:02.000
Quickly, man, unlock this cell.

23:02.000 --> 23:06.000
Mr. Clampett, on behalf of the entire city of Beverly Hills,

23:06.000 --> 23:11.000
I extend our deep and humble apologies for this unfortunate and embarrassing incident.

23:11.000 --> 23:15.000
Oh, I'm Mildred Drysdale, president of the Commerce Bank of Beverly Hills.

23:15.000 --> 23:18.000
My car is waiting to take you and your family to your new home.

23:18.000 --> 23:22.000
We want you to know how happy we are to have you, your handsome nephew,

23:22.000 --> 23:25.000
your lovely daughter, and your beautiful money.

23:25.000 --> 23:26.000
Mother.

23:38.000 --> 23:40.000
Wait a minute! Stop this car!

23:42.000 --> 23:44.000
Mr. Drysdale, you tricked us!

23:44.000 --> 23:47.000
You just took us out of jail so you could bring us back up here to prison!

23:47.000 --> 23:49.000
Head for the hills, everybody!

23:49.000 --> 23:51.000
No, wait! Come back!

23:51.000 --> 23:53.000
It's not a prison, it's your home!

23:54.000 --> 23:57.000
No, wait! Mr. Clampett! Listen to me!

23:57.000 --> 24:19.000
Wait! Come back!

24:19.000 --> 24:28.000
Well, now it's time to say goodbye to Jed and all his kin.

24:28.000 --> 24:31.000
They would like to thank you folks for kindly dropping in.

24:31.000 --> 24:35.000
You're all invited back next week to this locality

24:35.000 --> 24:38.000
to have a heaping helping of their hospitality.

24:38.000 --> 24:40.000
Little Billy, that is.

24:40.000 --> 24:43.000
Set a spell. Take your shoes off.

24:43.000 --> 24:49.000
We all come back now, dude.

